+Hey Attila, massive W getting OpenClaw fully running on Replit— that's some next-level hacking, legend status unlocked 😂. Running a full agent setup on Replit's free tier (or whatever plan) is clutch for quick tests/grinds, but yeah, the web_search tool is hardcoded to demand a Brave API key by default. The error you're seeing is exactly that: no key → tool fails, even if you try configuring it.
+
+From what the community/docs show (as of Feb 2026), **native built-in support for alternatives like SearXNG isn't fully baked into the core config for most versions**—it's either in pending PRs (#13334, #6876, etc.), or handled via plugins/skills, or custom hacks. Replit makes it trickier because:
+
+- No persistent Docker support on free/basic Replit (Docker compose for SearXNG won't run reliably without hacks or paid Always-On).
+- Replit's env is containerized but limited—no full root/systemd, ports can be finicky, and background services die on sleep/restarts.
+- Gateway/env vars are settable, but the tool expects Brave format.
+
+### Fastest Realistic Fixes for Replit
+Here are the top paths people are actually using in similar Replit/OpenClaw setups (prioritized by ease/speed on Replit):
+
+1. **Quickest Hack: Use a Public SearXNG Instance (No Self-Host Needed)**
+   - Many public SearXNG mirrors exist (privacy-focused, but use at own risk—some log, some rate-limit).
+   - Popular free ones right now: https://searx.space (pick one with good uptime, like searx.be or searx.tiekoetter.net).
+   - In Replit Shell, set env var or edit config to point there (if your modified OpenClaw supports custom provider/baseUrl).
+   - Manual config try (in your openclaw.json or via env):
+     ```json
+     "tools": {
+       "web": {
+         "search": {
+           "enabled": true,
+           "provider": "searxng",  // if supported in your fork/PR
+           "searxng": {
+             "baseUrl": "https://searx.be"  // or any public instance from https://searx.space
+           }
+         }
+       }
+     }
+     ```
+   - If "searxng" provider isn't recognized (common on older/base versions), set a fallback or use a skill (see below).
+   - Test: Restart gateway/agent, ask for a search → if it hits the URL with ?q=query&format=json, you're golden.
+
+2. **Install a SearXNG Skill/Plugin (Best Long-Term on Replit)**
+   - Community skills like "searxng-local" or "local-websearch" bypass the built-in web_search entirely and add a custom tool that calls SearXNG directly.
+   - In Replit Shell (assuming you have npm/openclaw CLI working):
+     ```
+     openclaw skills install searxng-local   # or from playbooks/lobehub repos, e.g. clockworksquirrel/searxng-local
+     ```
+     - Or if it's on GitHub/npm:
+       ```
+       npm install openclaw-skills-searxng-local  # adjust name based on exact repo
+       openclaw skills add searxng-local
+       ```
+   - Config: Set env var in Replit Secrets/Env tab:
+     - Key: `SEARXNG_URL`
+     - Value: `https://your-public-searxng-instance.com` (e.g., https://search.bus-hit.me)
+   - The skill description: Aggregates Google/DDG/Brave/etc. privately, no keys, JSON output compatible with agents.
+   - Agent will prefer/use this new tool for searches once installed/reloaded.
+
+3. **Tavily Plugin Alternative (If You Want AI-Optimized Results, Free Tier Exists)**
+   - Some folks swapped Brave → Tavily via plugin (github.com/framix-team/openclaw-tavily or similar).
+   - Steps:
+     - Get free Tavily key: https://app.tavily.com (sign up, grab API key—generous free credits for testing).
+     - In Shell:
+       ```
+       openclaw plugins install openclaw-tavily  # or npm install openclaw-tavily && openclaw plugins add
+       ```
+     - Add to Replit Secrets: `TAVILY_API_KEY=your_key_here`
+     - Restart → agent uses tavily_search as drop-in replacement (cleaner for money plays like trend/arbitrage spotting).
+
+4. **Nuclear: Fake Brave with a Proxy/Shim (Advanced, but Works on Replit)**
+   - Run a tiny Node/Flask proxy in another Replit tab that mimics Brave endpoint → routes to DDG/SearXNG.
+   - But Replit limits concurrent always-on stuff—better for testing.
+
+### Immediate Next Steps in Replit
+- Check your modified OpenClaw version: Run `openclaw --version` or look at package.json/git log. If it's recent (post-Feb 2026 PR merges), try `openclaw configure --section web` anyway—some forks added "searxng" or "custom".
+- Set env var `BRAVE_API_KEY=fake` temporarily (some setups skip validation if present).
+- If stuck, paste the exact error after trying a public SearXNG URL or skill install.
+- Pro move: Fork your Replit → add a simple Express server that proxies /search to a public SearXNG, then point config baseUrl to localhost:port.
+
